<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saif bin Sultan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1711">1711</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Saif ibn Sultan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saif bin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> from 1692 to 1711, the most powerful ruler of the Ya'aruba dynasty. He built up a strong navy, and in 1698 his forces took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-jesus">Fort Jesus</a> at Mombasa from the Portuguese after a long siege, extending Omani influence along the East African coast. At home he invested in falaj irrigation channels and date plantations, and he was buried at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rustaq">Rustaq</a>.</p></div>
